se-infra', 'omnibase-spi', 'omnimarket']\n    [deploy-gateway] ERROR: Sibling lock-pin preflight FAILED.\n\nThat is the only deploy path for the omninode-gateway lane, and workspace mode\nis the only mode that can carry unreleased dev code -- which is exactly what\nwas needed on 2026-09-06 to ship #3221 (d8833a7f) to the forwarder whose\noutbound cloud leg had been wedged 8768s across 294 reconnects on\n\"outbound payload tenant_id does not match attached tenant\".\n\nThe regression test asserts the script's --repo set against\ncheck_sibling_lock_pins.py's own accepted-package map rather than a copied\nliteral, so the two cannot drift apart again silently. RED on the unpatched\nscript (unknown: ['onex-change-control']), GREEN after.\n\nOMN-17201","verified_at":"2026-09-06T10:13:55Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/2ea74bc4de7623456bb20f303391ca2b2361a922","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commit/2ea74bc4de7623456bb20f303391ca2b2361a922","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/2ea74bc4de7623456bb20f303391ca2b2361a922/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c6c4af89a0f6bcc56cd97bc7940830930e354ad5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/c6c4af89a0f6bcc56cd97bc7940830930e354ad5","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commit/c6c4af89a0f6bcc56cd97bc7940830930e354ad5"}]},"status":"ahead","ahead_by":9,"behind_by":0,"total_commits":9,"commits":[{"sha":"4cff0618ae1a6f0f420d5aea13c6f2bf0715cbb6","node_id":"C_kwDOPuAjtNoAKDRjZmYwNjE4YWUxYTZmMGY0MjBkNWFlYTEzYzZmMmJmMDcxNWNiYjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-09-06T11:59:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-06T11:59:46Z"},"message":"fix(OMN-17985): refuse an unregistered RUNTIME_PROFILE instead of silently falling back (#3238)\n\nRUNTIME_PROFILE was read twice by two code paths that disagreed about what it\nresolved to. load_runtime_profile fell back to the \"default\" profile with a\nwarning, discarding the role identity the value carries. The auto-wiring\nownership filter never consulted that resolved profile at all -- it read the\nraw env string. An unregistered value matches no contract's declared\nruntime_profiles list AND is != \"main\", so every contract is skipped: the\nmanifest empties, zero subscriptions are wired, and the process still passes\nreadiness. The only signal was one warning from a different function.\n\n- load_runtime_profile now raises ProtocolConfigurationError on an unknown\n  name, naming the value and listing the known profiles. Unset/blank still\n  resolves to \"default\"; that is \"unset\", not \"unknown\".\n- resolve_runtime_profile_name() is the single validated read for ownership\n  decisions. Its unset fallback is \"main\", exactly the value the ownership\n  filter already used -- consolidating adds validation, it does not move a\n  default. Twelve raw reads across service_kernel and runtime_host_process now\n  go through it, including the boot banner, which defaulted to \"default\" while\n  every ownership read defaulted to \"main\" and so could name a role the process\n  was not wiring as.\n- Dockerfile.runtime shipped RUNTIME_PROFILE=all as an image default: a stale\n  service-selection value from an older meaning of this variable. Any container\n  from that image not overriding it wired zero contracts. Now \"main\".\n\n_current_runtime_profile_name in runtime_host_process deliberately keeps its\nown \"default\" fallback -- it matches operator-written enabled_profiles lists,\nso moving that fallback would be a gating change, not a validation change. It\nis safe because an unregistered value can no longer reach a booted runtime.\n\nRED first: the new test module failed at import (no resolve_runtime_profile_name)\nand the pre-existing test_unknown_runtime_profile_still_falls_back_to_default is\ninverted here -- the behaviour it pinned is the defect.","tree":{"sha":"abf5ed5e15442cecaa8da261e022fb404193d02c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/git/trees/abf5ed5e15442cecaa8da261e022fb404193d02c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/git/commits/4cff0618ae1a6f0f420d5aea13c6f2bf0715cbb6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnVWyCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUikQACOZ3g0nOcdHgGgxap410LBq\nY90FChyA/vM0g1vgbl9hZEIQ/GlNrX8kYdHzqOyCUYx6mTkM5MGEibRzxf0EB9Qn\nu1rbwlvJ+r6YLtbOHZg8OxCj18RgzkXRS8s8wLmVGE+i/2AZi3lr4TYh9sQHJeZo\n6D9Y0KBWn0d7SyOQGOf7qZYE6399Wr/d4iJNHbwmCZ2Pf6J6Nik8Ei+ge6H0N35/\nl9tI4g6KZ3BOneSq3XyL3OqUNmxBlY7VttBwlmDEOCiPk0y8yPAqiZ8m8Aeq6sgv\napUdBgKbvuiPArI7Rb9QNlOpZPObRqtLzzM3YpnkrdKz3XK/Lj34MEAlsmztTn6L\nD4A9eFFJ1gGU6AwXzYI+lwgIJf2S/YjYIzvyRy5EDfzHRt1ppwhKhvBzqtNqWLqw\nPbD081X+lHnh/VzTOZFH0KhQJJbiPPoBTJlmym2HqntmOoKbNvXwfkT2GwH6kYhk\niq19FH9L+VykZIPl0JYJG1aAgJ2kfm7qeNSHEgrhubGmAGgPPf8drY8kW05QmvyZ\nW0AaHhO4FxdrVwL349srN6TV+P12ZWZLAJb/adBHjAah1Z0RtwP4p1bbkxe3mN+u\nEHmabF1fJX/Rw70J2wai2NULR09OQzx0DWCXCnqThTqgzSLVDSFIzFz7Zn/VrCr6\noOq5hqeVZ3N60HyIbdoY\n=/ZJu\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree abf5ed5e15442cecaa8da261e022fb404193d02c\nparent 2ea74bc4de7623456bb20f303391ca2b2361a922\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1788695986 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788695986 +0000\n\nfix(OMN-17985): refuse an unregistered RUNTIME_PROFILE instead of silently falling back (#3238)\n\nRUNTIME_PROFILE was read twice by two code paths that disagreed about what it\nresolved to. load_runtime_profile fell back to the \"default\" profile with a\nwarning, discarding the role identity the value carries. The auto-wiring\nownership filter never consulted that resolved profile at all -- it read the\nraw env string. An unregistered value matches no contract's declared\nruntime_profiles list AND is != \"main\", so every contract is skipped: the\nmanifest empties, zero subscriptions are wired, and the process still passes\nreadiness. The only signal was one warning from a different function.\n\n- load_runtime_profile now raises ProtocolConfigurationError on an unknown\n  name, naming the value and listing the known profiles. Unset/blank still\n  resolves to \"default\"; that is \"unset\", not \"unknown\".\n- resolve_runtime_profile_name() is the single validated read for ownership\n  decisions. Its unset fallback is \"main\", exactly the value the ownership\n  filter already used -- consolidating adds validation, it does not move a\n  default. Twelve raw reads across service_kernel and runtime_host_process now\n  go through it, including the boot banner, which defaulted to \"default\" while\n  every ownership read defaulted to \"main\" and so could name a role the process\n  was not wiring as.\n- Dockerfile.runtime shipped RUNTIME_PROFILE=all as an image default: a stale\n  service-selection value from an older meaning of this variable. Any container\n  from that image not overriding it wired zero contracts. Now \"main\".\n\n_current_runtime_profile_name in runtime_host_process deliberately keeps its\nown \"default\" fallback -- it matches operator-written enabled_profiles lists,\nso moving that fallback would be a gating change, not a validation change. It\nis safe because an unregistered value can no longer reach a booted runtime.\n\nRED first: the new test module failed at import (no resolve_runtime_profile_name)\nand the pre-existing test_unknown_runtime_profile_still_falls_back_to_default is\ninverted here -- the behaviour it pinned is the defect.","verified_at":"2026-09-06T11:59:47Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/4cff0618ae1a6f0f420d5aea13c6f2bf0715cbb6","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commit/4cff0618ae1a6f0f420d5aea13c6f2bf0715cbb6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/4cff0618ae1a6f0f420d5aea13c6f2bf0715cbb6/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2ea74bc4de7623456bb20f303391ca2b2361a922","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/2ea74bc4de7623456bb20f303391ca2b2361a922","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commit/2ea74bc4de7623456bb20f303391ca2b2361a922"}]},{"sha":"6fa976af1511e82097ee7aeeeb13b663c6f14ab0","node_id":"C_kwDOPuAjtNoAKDZmYTk3NmFmMTUxMWU4MjA5N2VlN2FlZWViMTNiNjYzYzZmMTRhYjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"onexbot-occ-writer[bot]","email":"307849072+onexbot-occ-writer[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-09-06T13:17:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-06T13:17:12Z"},"message":"chore(OMN-17292): advance omnimarket contract pin to 74bec0ef5a63 [bot] (#3239)\n\nCo-authored-by: omninode-bot <bot@omninode.ai>","tree":{"sha":"a6453b9cbedd37644de7a83654762bf49ab59fc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/git/trees/a6453b9cbedd37644de7a83654762bf49ab59fc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/git/commits/6fa976af1511e82097ee7aeeeb13b663c6f14ab0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnWfYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAklEQAGX/Y7hHXICDQrJyrzXBnbMx\nrQhiX5cg0bYt67L0ZnMyC/YBYAb9O8NvtXLu+65FfvwuOBnbShhnS6e085bK+RB+\nppTki7SK09gdtr+WOBpM1esiBVgNzR9lcsEbz7n4edNpsTdFe2QNsG0fETOk3UC+\ny7v67L0KMAvY+TDa0SYOvPM7OgszBI9FV3SJoDgTwtWjhySHJ4kM64se/9zelLs/\nlfbpvuwQzz9nxRCHkPwDqjlyOY3BCPCII+TeSTNlliYk6v6iYHVFAGxEJ61mdh2c\nxu9ouB/fha8LYaevNEFvUyMqzX6Kz1r4eOCa51ihLfJdulDKrcct0ZfORMgHJ9Lm\ndIiujEduyYCLthyaW4BhmWQTiq5bFd56IStbOG4mT7avlogz6VqhHpoR3xwZmSJ8\nJC3LMLzUVSehC22viELMI8Tz+LrC4GZbi/UJt21LOKuPWytrsBZR6GW4LgbZN/jS\nM19iEsHcWz0EMzG9uaD6duXr0zr5nEt7cXNU/604VDfyrHYWbKWERJKWsjumA9hJ\n+uAN77Joeup8fIyjZu+ZQ2tNC7FLNHHKm99HhKq3TSz9v6i8bnk8VVL9Xc5J2qqW\nNbNrxci6kdQrTX3Q/wKcuppfBS1fxo6KdSbACqIc8eIycoPNYykc7hNQD0cYQLLL\nBPr354INRQZxlZf8zIfq\n=wjJw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a6453b9cbedd37644de7a83654762bf49ab59fc7\nparent 4cff0618ae1a6f0f420d5aea13c6f2bf0715cbb6\nauthor onexbot-occ-writer[bot] <307849072+onexbot-occ-writer[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1788700632 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788700632 -0400\n\nchore(OMN-17292): advance omnimarket contract pin to 74bec0ef5a63 [bot] (#3239)\n\nCo-authored-by: omninode-bot <bot@omninode.ai>","verified_at":"2026-09-06T13:17:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/6fa976af1511e82097ee7aeeeb13b663c6f14ab0","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commit/6fa976af1511e82097ee7aeeeb13b663c6f14ab0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/6fa976af1511e82097ee7aeeeb13b663c6f14ab0/comments","author":{"login":"onexbot-occ-writer[bot]","id":307849072,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOEllncA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209038818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/onexbot-occ-writer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/onexbot-occ-writer%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4cff0618ae1a6f0f420d5aea13c6f2bf0715cbb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/4cff0618ae1a6f0f420d5aea13c6f2bf0715cbb6","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commit/4cff0618ae1a6f0f420d5aea13c6f2bf0715cbb6"}]},{"sha":"f9326a95b757aa8659ce7e9582ad6f42a6e4a614","node_id":"C_kwDOPuAjtNoAKGY5MzI2YTk1Yjc1N2FhODY1OWNlN2U5NTgyYWQ2ZjQyYTZlNGE2MTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-09-06T13:22:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-06T13:22:11Z"},"message":"feat(OMN-17863): provision Node + corepack on the evidence-autoclose sweep (#3240)\n\nEvery provisioning step in `evidence-autoclose-sweep.yml` is Python-shaped —\nsetup-python, setup-uv, a lock-exact gate venv, a separate dispatch venv,\nper-repo `uv sync` in the OMN-16902 materialise step — because until now every\nbehaviour check under adjudication was.\n\nThe behaviour proof drafted on OMN-17863 is not: `check_type: test_passes` /\n`check_value: \"pnpm test:audit-verdict\"` / `cwd: ${OMNI_HOME}/omniweb`.\n`test_passes` is a semantic alias for `command` (OMN-16824) — dod_verify runs\nthe declared string raw in its declared cwd — so on this job it is exit 127,\nrecorded `failed=1`. That asserts a product defect on the strength of the\nverifier's own missing runtime, and reads in a receipt exactly like the product\ngenuinely failing its proof. It is also strictly more blocking than the missing\nproof it would replace, which is why the author held the check unpushed rather\nthan landing it into a job that could not execute it. Nothing establishes an\nambient Node either: this repo has zero workflows that use pnpm, and omniweb's\nown CI obtains it through pnpm/action-setup + setup-node on every run.\n\nThree steps, placed after the materialise step so the version is derived from\nthe JS projects that were actually cloned rather than hardcoded here where it\nwould drift invisibly:\n\n- derive the Node version from each materialised destination's own `.nvmrc`\n  (the more specific statement) then `engines.node`, taking the highest floor\n  across the set because one runtime has to satisfy all of them. Falls back to\n  the workflow-level NODE_VERSION_DEFAULT when nothing declares one, so a\n  window with no JS contract in scope is not blocked by the absence of a JS\n  requirement. Executed against the real workspace before landing: omniweb +\n  omnibase_infra -> version=22.13 (from omniweb engines.node >=22.13); empty\n  input -> version=22, with the reason printed.\n- actions/setup-node pinned to a 40-hex sha, matching the bar actions/checkout\n  already meets in this job.\n- `corepack enable` in its own step, because setup-node does not enable corepack\n  and does not ship pnpm — Node alone is the same exit 127 by a different route.\n  corepack is what makes a project's `packageManager` pin the thing that\n  actually runs, which is the property the staged toolchain in node_dod_verify\n  resolves against. Both versions are echoed, since provisioning that reports\n  success without being usable is the failure this repo keeps re-learning\n  (OMN-17307).\n\nBoth steps that dispatch dod_verify — the sweep and the opt-in diagnose step —\nget DOD_VERIFY_HERMETIC_NODE_ROOT under RUNNER_TEMP (a real node_modules is\nhundreds of megabytes and inside GITHUB_WORKSPACE would be walked by the\ngate-venv purity assertions), DOD_VERIFY_HERMETIC_SYNC_TIMEOUT_S=900 (the\ninstall is a download and must not be charged to this job's 180s per-check\nceiling, which would record CHECK_BUDGET_EXCEEDED — a verifier-side ceiling\nreported as a fact about the ticket, OMN-17795), and\nCOREPACK_ENABLE_DOWNLOAD_PROMPT=0 (a scheduled run has nobody to answer a\nprompt). The diagnose step exists to reproduce the sweep's environment exactly;\na toolchain present for one and not the other would make the diagnostic lie\nabout the thing it exists to diagnose.\n\nEnforcement: tests/ci/test_autoclose_node_toolchain_omn17863.py, 8 cases, all\nRED before this change.\n\nProducer side is omnimarket#2330 (the staged lock-exact JS toolchain in\nnode_dod_verify), which lands first because this job installs omnimarket from\ndev.","tree":{"sha":"95812a272f7a08e42700f78bfed1d8033f0288c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/git/trees/95812a272f7a08e42700f78bfed1d8033f0288c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/git/commits/f9326a95b757aa8659ce7e9582ad6f42a6e4a614","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnWkDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZ58QACVSnPM90bCSnn1yoMJohmb8\nfEtj5uM6zDjXYBK1hetNeC7kX3C6mmNPaC/FrnxzwN6i2QnQeG56X4Tvjdj1CmCz\nm3o098kdmlHcw353NekjEUaPmp8aa1u/Y0SN6pq0Iwe4DbNoFLh9OTOQ7HshDMGa\ndcBo4mh1GEbtcRh8k38jlsbPjiU7XkcalzBlpj39nig2BmLtZz6jFZvBxKTjRWYu\n2OZIKtwcV4c+lsyxJu0EfaRdX7pB5S5qfq1Oo1kHOwRC1husMZQcOUDDE+sSmOR5\n2cugatwJVZaW8gWDGSyeCGYWqeLUoLXYMLA3sgWfoGfuV8dKueC1ksTMFFUcHD8q\nfad43/AW0gzu6lSZKM4WHpWSzQ3PTvex11yNYVZkrkO094/bLIBo3e8EFYU9sZvJ\nAWLgZ6Y6FjaG3+xIOicU0o22vzAZG+K3fnjsaGS/xKeswfOYq75OI+7tPfx4EVoS\nkT6zUxZgAeDUp9yrrEqzDeYctfkymQ8a4eSbNyzEJsHriobsDSpFz2Sz2x+felXj\nPL0xHz3pDwU3/U18fi33HbNzODtsnQBt+shstu5K2STH29GLHnQxByvh5+2igwHO\n0lcdbG/2qB4mVoK9c3emG7iRqCJzzmTmC7ZCaomm0KsUFqy0jfng83h/UshiCMio\ndaxpdLhUhkiUrFg1tbsI\n=OcVK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 95812a272f7a08e42700f78bfed1d8033f0288c4\nparent 6fa976af1511e82097ee7aeeeb13b663c6f14ab0\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1788700931 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788700931 +0000\n\nfeat(OMN-17863): provision Node + corepack on the evidence-autoclose sweep (#3240)\n\nEvery provisioning step in `evidence-autoclose-sweep.yml` is Python-shaped —\nsetup-python, setup-uv, a lock-exact gate venv, a separate dispatch venv,\nper-repo `uv sync` in the OMN-16902 materialise step — because until now every\nbehaviour check under adjudication was.\n\nThe behaviour proof drafted on OMN-17863 is not: `check_type: test_passes` /\n`check_value: \"pnpm test:audit-verdict\"` / `cwd: ${OMNI_HOME}/omniweb`.\n`test_passes` is a semantic alias for `command` (OMN-16824) — dod_verify runs\nthe declared string raw in its declared cwd — so on this job it is exit 127,\nrecorded `failed=1`. That asserts a product defect on the strength of the\nverifier's own missing runtime, and reads in a receipt exactly like the product\ngenuinely failing its proof. It is also strictly more blocking than the missing\nproof it would replace, which is why the author held the check unpushed rather\nthan landing it into a job that could not execute it. Nothing establishes an\nambient Node either: this repo has zero workflows that use pnpm, and omniweb's\nown CI obtains it through pnpm/action-setup + setup-node on every run.\n\nThree steps, placed after the materialise step so the version is derived from\nthe JS projects that were actually cloned rather than hardcoded here where it\nwould drift invisibly:\n\n- derive the Node version from each materialised destination's own `.nvmrc`\n  (the more specific statement) then `engines.node`, taking the highest floor\n  across the set because one runtime has to satisfy all of them. Falls back to\n  the workflow-level NODE_VERSION_DEFAULT when nothing declares one, so a\n  window with no JS contract in scope is not blocked by the absence of a JS\n  requirement. Executed against the real workspace before landing: omniweb +\n  omnibase_infra -> version=22.13 (from omniweb engines.node >=22.13); empty\n  input -> version=22, with the reason printed.\n- actions/setup-node pinned to a 40-hex sha, matching the bar actions/checkout\n  already meets in this job.\n- `corepack enable` in its own step, because setup-node does not enable corepack\n  and does not ship pnpm — Node alone is the same exit 127 by a different route.\n  corepack is what makes a project's `packageManager` pin the thing that\n  actually runs, which is the property the staged toolchain in node_dod_verify\n  resolves against. Both versions are echoed, since provisioning that reports\n  success without being usable is the failure this repo keeps re-learning\n  (OMN-17307).\n\nBoth steps that dispatch dod_verify — the sweep and the opt-in diagnose step —\nget DOD_VERIFY_HERMETIC_NODE_ROOT under RUNNER_TEMP (a real node_modules is\nhundreds of megabytes and inside GITHUB_WORKSPACE would be walked by the\ngate-venv purity assertions), DOD_VERIFY_HERMETIC_SYNC_TIMEOUT_S=900 (the\ninstall is a download and must not be charged to this job's 180s per-check\nceiling, which would record CHECK_BUDGET_EXCEEDED — a verifier-side ceiling\nreported as a fact about the ticket, OMN-17795), and\nCOREPACK_ENABLE_DOWNLOAD_PROMPT=0 (a scheduled run has nobody to answer a\nprompt). The diagnose step exists to reproduce the sweep's environment exactly;\na toolchain present for one and not the other would make the diagnostic lie\nabout the thing it exists to diagnose.\n\nEnforcement: tests/ci/test_autoclose_node_toolchain_omn17863.py, 8 cases, all\nRED before this change.\n\nProducer side is omnimarket#2330 (the staged lock-exact JS toolchain in\nnode_dod_verify), which lands first because this job installs omnimarket from\ndev.","verified_at":"2026-09-06T13:22:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/f9326a95b757aa8659ce7e9582ad6f42a6e4a614","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commit/f9326a95b757aa8659ce7e9582ad6f42a6e4a614","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/f9326a95b757aa8659ce7e9582ad6f42a6e4a614/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-